### What issue are you seeing?

When running through a list of changes in an application suddenly Codex started revisiting all previous changes (unrelated to the ask).  You can see from the prompt I'm asking to improve the location service, after a few lines it starts revisiting things like pallet and other seemingly unrelated already resolved asks.

This ran out my usage and I hit my limits.  I found this strange, went back and looked and it had actually been doing this for quite some time, I would issue a prompt it would revisit lots of apparently unrelated prompts, then finally execute the prompt I asked for.

"I'll also fix a typo (pallet to palette), make sure error logging and location updates
  in the profile work correctly, and verify that theme preferences are properly stored, loaded, and sent
  through the profile service. " -> There was no ask to "Fix a typo, nor to verify theme preferences"

